    content: `**Bashkir (Башҡорт теле)** is a Turkic language spoken by ~1.2 million people, primarily in the Republic of Bashkortostan, Russia.

**Key Features:**
• **Agglutinative** — Suffixes stack onto roots (one word can be a sentence!)
• **Vowel Harmony** — Suffixes must match the root's vowel type
• **SOV Word Order** — Subject-Object-Verb (opposite of English)
• **No Articles** — No "a" or "the" (Bashkir doesn't need them!)
• **No Grammatical Gender** — "ул" means he/she/it
• **Postpositions** — Location words come AFTER the noun

**The Alphabet:** Cyrillic + 9 special letters:
Ә ә, Ө ө, Ү ү (front vowels)
Ҡ ҡ, Ғ ғ, Ҙ ҙ, Һ һ, Ң ң (special consonants)

**Comparison with Turkish:**
Many words are cognate! балыҡ/balık (fish), ат/at (horse), су/һыу (water)`
